\ Both names are words the linter imports, and neither is in the base scope, so running this file
\ raises nothing and linting it reports no shadow. `all-words` would report both. So would its
\ native entries alone, which still hold `make-lint-rule`, a native `struct{` constructor.

\\ Named like the linter's own constructor.
make-lint-rule: ( a b c d -- r ) [ 3drop ] ;

\\ Named like a linter word.
format-diagnostic: ( d -- s ) [ drop "" ] ;
